OpenWRT's root filesystem is squashfs which is already read-only by nature. chattr is meaningless on squashfs and on overlayfs. The immutability is architectural — squashfs cannot be written to at all. The overlay on top is jffs2 or ext4 depending on your build. So the protection model is different from standard Linux.

