So apk add openvpn now shows operation not permitted..  how to fix
May 18

OpenWRT moved from opkg to apk in recent snapshot builds. The operation not permitted on apk means the filesystem is mounted read-only or the overlay isn't writable.
bash

# Check what's happening
mount | grep -E 'overlay|root|/'
df -h
# Is overlay mounted rw?

# Check overlay specifically
mount | grep overlay
# Should show: overlayfs on / type overlay (rw,...)
# If ro — that's your problem

bash

# Check if overlay has space
df -h /overlay
# If full, apk can't write package database

bash

# Most common fix — remount overlay rw
mount -o remount,rw /overlay 2>/dev/null
mount -o remount,rw / 2>/dev/null

# Then retry
apk update
apk add openvpn-openssl

bash

# If that fails check apk lock file
ls -la /lib/apk/db/lock
# If lock file exists from crashed install:
rm -f /lib/apk/db/lock
apk update
apk add openvpn-openssl

bash

# If overlay is genuinely full
df -h /overlay
# Free space by removing unused packages
apk list --installed
apk del <anything_unused>

# Check what's eating overlay space
du -sh /overlay/upper/* 2>/dev/null | sort -rh | head -20

bash

# Nuclear option if overlay is corrupt
# This resets overlay — loses all config changes
# ONLY if nothing else works and you have config backed up
firstboot
reboot

bash

# After successful apk add — verify
apk info openvpn-openssl
which openvpn
openvpn --version

